# Floor-exhaustiveness A+C waiver roster -- MATERIALIZED INPUT DATA.
#
# One structural site key per line: "<module_path>::<declaration>::<scrutinee>".
# The seed-Rust A+C waiver arm in cli_run/compile_clean.rs reads the file that the
# environment variable GUNBC_EXHAUSTIVENESS_UNKNOWN_ALLOWLIST names, trims each
# line, and ignores blank lines and lines beginning with '#'. A line present here
# makes the arm treat that site's ExhaustivenessUnknown as advisory instead of
# hard-blocking emission.
#
# This file is DERIVED data. Its single authority is
# v2.workflow.floor_exhaustiveness_allowlist.floor_exhaustiveness_allowlist(); the
# producer v2.workflow.floor_exhaustiveness_allowlist_data_file is the sole writer of
# these lines. Consistency between this file and that roster is ENFORCED, not
# promised, by
# test.claim.floor_exhaustiveness_allowlist_equality_witness.floor_exhaustiveness_data_file_equals_the_roster
# (both directions): a line here that is not a rostered site waives a site the
# operator never authorized -> RED; a rostered site missing here lets it block ->
# RED. Authorized by the operator's A+C ruling; no more exceptions.
